        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for kind words!\r\n\r\n> I notice though that by default the `StatusLine` highlight looks almost like the `Normal`. Is it intentional? I would like to suggest using the same background as `StatusLineNC`, and change the foreground colour instead to something with higher contrast\r\n\r\nBackground of `StatusLine` is [accent with background lightness](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/afa6f0a3dc27b910501651f5fc26ef3b551fd99b/lua/mini/hues.lua#L705). By default accent uses background hue, so this appears the same as `Normal`.\r\n\r\nThis is intentional. If you want something different, I'd suggest using custom accent or override `StatusLine` manually (maybe inside `ColorScheme` event).\r\n \r\n> I'm also thinking of submitting a PR with values for `hl-User1..9`, but I would like to know if you agree that changing only the foreground makes sense.\r\n\r\nI am not sure the whole `hl-User1..9` is a good idea, as it seems to mostly be reserved to be defined by the user (as name suggests). I can't remember seeing recent-ish color scheme defining those.",
            "created_at": "2023-05-31T16:27:55Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/319#issuecomment-1570547682",
            "id": 1570547682,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/319",
            "minimized": null,
