        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Background of StatusLine is [accent with background lightness](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/afa6f0a3dc27b910501651f5fc26ef3b551fd99b/lua/mini/hues.lua#L705). By default accent uses background hue, so this appears the same as Normal\r\n\r\nRight, I noticed that. Would it be possible to adjust the `accent` for `randomhue`? I already tried setting it up, but it's ignored. I haven't dived into the code that much, so I'm not sure if what I'm asking would be possible. In any case, I already use `ColorScheme` to adjust some stuff, so I will go that route for now\r\n\r\n> I am not sure the whole `hl-User1..9` is a good idea, as it seems to mostly be reserved to be defined by the user (as name suggests). I can't remember seeing recent-ish color scheme defining those.\r\n\r\nThis may be weird, but I always wanted schemes to define those, so I could just use them 😅 But fair enough, `ColorScheme` is the way to go!",
            "created_at": "2023-05-31T18:29:50Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/319#issuecomment-1570714681",
