        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Right, I noticed that. Would it be possible to adjust the `accent` for `randomhue`? I already tried setting it up, but it's ignored. I haven't dived into the code that much, so I'm not sure if what I'm asking would be possible. In any case, I already use `ColorScheme` to adjust some stuff, so I will go that route for now\r\n\r\nNot for the 'randomhue' per se, but you can create your own randomhue-like color scheme with different background:\r\n- Create file 'colors/my_randomhue.lua' in your home config directory ('~/.config/nvim/' if you are on Unix).\r\n- Copy lines from [original 'randomhue'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/colors/randomhue.lua).\r\n- Change `saturation` option to your liking. Also I'd recommend changing `vim.g.colors_name = 'my_randomhue'`.\r\n- Source it with `:colorscheme my_randomhue`.",
            "created_at": "2023-05-31T18:40:45Z",
